silm:instances_papers_05_granite_substrate_chapters_01_storage_as_leg_sections_04_colimit_above_granite_concrete_anchor silm:hasExample "In 'ColimitAboveGraniteConcreteAnchor', the bare-symbol→anchor table grounds the abstract symbols in the Tartu-Animal-Clinic / Mittens-2026-05-18 domain story. For example, the governed Mittens individual — the colimit assembled from all typed legs: type (Cat), domestic-cat refinement, taxonomy (Felis catus/TSN 183798), evidence (vet record), quality (4.3 kg), process (annual exam), role (clinic patient), storage (Icechunk chunk); also, nodes in the full Granite olog that are not storage nodes: Mittens (apex), Cat, DomesticCat, VetCarePlan_77, taxonomy nodes, evidence nodes, quality/measurement nodes; also, the cocone legs from each source-diagram object to the Mittens apex: type leg from Cat node, taxonomy leg from Felis catus/TSN 183798 node, evidence leg from vet-record node, quality leg from body-mass node, storage leg from ChunkManifest node." .
